WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:10.048
SpareCycle joins a refurbishment coordinator's planning workflow with a diagnostics engineer's code review. Follow the working product, recorded backend proof, and the investment gates.

2
00:00:10.728 --> 00:00:20.480
A technician records an observation. An engineer defines a supported software issue. A separate reviewer inspects the tested candidate. Every handoff keeps its evidence.

3
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:30.513
Pilot Operations freezes the validated plan, then records per-device progress, blockers, assignment and due dates, actual effort, costs and evidence-backed manual checks.

4
00:00:30.693 --> 00:00:40.926
A local scorecard distinguishes proposed devices from technician-reported outcomes. Export a handoff or backup. These records neither consume shared stock nor certify a physical release.

5
00:00:41.606 --> 00:00:52.188
A public model question invokes Tavily in the application backend. The server filters official documentation, assigns source IDs, and passes only bounded snippets to NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius.

6
00:00:52.368 --> 00:01:01.531
The result shows its sources, uncertainties and next checks. A matched citation is not a hardware diagnosis: the technician must inspect the source and the actual device.

7
00:01:02.211 --> 00:01:07.369
The company workspace connects a passport, project, and change request to a particular evidence revision.

8
00:01:07.549 --> 00:01:14.992
These records and accounts are synthetic. The provider calls, test executions, and resulting draft pull requests actually happened.

9
00:01:15.672 --> 00:01:21.296
Here, a valid zero-percent battery reading becomes missing data. That can mislead diagnosis.

10
00:01:21.476 --> 00:01:28.899
The request defines expected behavior before generation. The backend compares original and candidate code using exactly the same test cases.

11
00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:36.817
These saved private-run timestamps document Nano investigation, passing verification, Super review, and a draft created after separate approval.

12
00:01:36.997 --> 00:01:43.050
This is recorded execution evidence. The intervals include pauses, so they are not a latency benchmark.

13
00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:55.727
Nebius Token Factory hosts inference. NVIDIA supplies Nemotron. GitHub Actions executes tests; Supabase protects organization records. These are distinct services, each with a defined job.

14
00:01:56.407 --> 00:02:06.550
Nano and Lightning can investigate. Super writes and freshly reviews non-Ultra cases. Ultra is an explicit operator-enabled escalation, not an automatic promise of better quality.

15
00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:14.928
The supplied usage view records all four tiers. Its rounded cost buckets are provider evidence, not an exact invoice or comparative benchmark.

16
00:02:15.608 --> 00:02:23.506
The harness bounds evidence, requires structured output, and validates changes. The model has no shell, network, or publishing tool.

17
00:02:23.686 --> 00:02:30.564
Trusted server code controls testing and publication. The model proposes; the application authorizes each transition.

18
00:02:31.244 --> 00:02:40.072
A model stage has a forty-second deadline, a bounded context, strict output and reserved spend. There is no automatic paid retry after an uncertain result.

19
00:02:40.752 --> 00:02:50.230
Evidence revision, repository commit and candidate hashes travel together. Changed inputs require fresh verification and approval; a passing test cannot bless another patch.

20
00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:57.193
GitHub Actions executes both versions in a network-disabled container. The original has one failure and three passes.

21
00:02:57.373 --> 00:03:04.321
The candidate passes all four unchanged test cases. That proves covered behavior, not every input or hardware condition.

22
00:03:05.001 --> 00:03:10.970
The model reviewer receives fresh context. A different organization member approves the exact tested candidate.

23
00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:18.798
The private pilot rejected self-approval. The QA accounts are synthetic; this demonstrates a permission boundary, not customer adoption.

24
00:03:19.478 --> 00:03:26.201
This actual App-created draft contains the tested patch and verification metadata. Technician narratives remain in the workspace.

25
00:03:26.381 --> 00:03:31.595
A maintainer still reviews the code. Nothing is automatically merged or marked physically repaired.

26
00:03:32.275 --> 00:03:42.477
The private pilot used Nano investigation and Super patching and review. Encrypted source went to a pinned verifier in the same private repository. Independent approval preceded the real draft.

27
00:03:43.157 --> 00:03:50.220
Software can proceed to a bounded patch. Hardware goes to workshop review. Missing evidence calls for more evidence.

28
00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:55.808
The classification is implemented; only the software branch is demonstrated by the completed live fixture.

29
00:03:56.488 --> 00:04:08.246
The Workshop allocates declared parts, time and budget. It stays browser-local; authenticated Review has separate organization records. Their handoff is explicit, without automatic inventory synchronization.

30
00:04:08.926 --> 00:04:18.543
Review insights compare loaded evidence revisions, verification references and approval bindings. Filters bring stale records, delayed jobs and cases requiring attention into one queue.

31
00:04:18.723 --> 00:04:28.281
This is read-only guidance. It does not rerun tests, validate repository head, change permissions, or execute a job. Refresh the server record before deciding.

32
00:04:28.961 --> 00:04:37.374
An outsider organization request was rejected. LangSmith traces keep metadata, excluding source and diagnostic narratives from trace inputs and outputs.

33
00:04:37.554 --> 00:04:43.002
These are specific controls and checks. An independent security assessment is still future work.

34
00:04:43.682 --> 00:04:53.829
Start with one owned diagnostics project, one reproducible failure and a separate reviewer. A supervised pilot and usage-capped subscription are commercial hypotheses that still need buyer validation.

35
00:04:54.509 --> 00:05:05.536
Google sign-in works. Company email is deferred; managed SSO requires enforcement and deprovisioning. Broader runners and physical repair outcomes need additional implementation and real field measurement.

36
00:05:06.216 --> 00:05:18.504
Fund reliable onboarding and supervised pilots first. Then failure recovery, usage reconciliation and evaluations. Enforced SSO, shared stock and broader runner profiles follow only after their acceptance gates.

37
00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:31.196
Measure accepted fixes, regressions, review time and total cost, including rejected attempts. The selected two hundred roadmap capabilities are planned work with acceptance criteria, not two hundred shipped features.

38
00:05:31.876 --> 00:05:41.388
Inspect the live application, public draft, backend ledger, project dossier and roadmap. SpareCycle uses actual Nebius and NVIDIA inference to make the next action reviewable.
